class:: BlipSeries
summary:: Finite arithmetic series of partial frequencies
categories:: UGens>Generators>Deterministic
related:: Guides/BlipExtensions, Classes/BlipAD, Classes/BlipDecay, Classes/BlipDiff, Classes/BlipDisp, Classes/BlipFB, Classes/BlipFrac, Classes/BlipInt, Classes/BlipKernel, Classes/BlipPM, Classes/BlipPeak, Classes/BlipPower, Classes/BlipWidth

description::

BlipSeries averages partials at ratios code::first + (k * spacing):: for
code::k = 0 .. numPartials - 1::. It evaluates the arithmetic cosine series in
constant cost and keeps independent double-precision accumulators for the
first-partial phase and inter-partial phase.

The highest ratio limits the partial count below a 0.999-Nyquist margin.
Negative code::freq:: reverses both accumulators; zero frequency holds them.
Negative code::first:: or code::spacing:: is clamped to zero, and
code::spacing == 0:: is a single coincident sinusoid. Topology changes fade
over one block. The output is peak-normalized by the retained partial count.

The closest vanilla UGen is link::Classes/Blip::. With code::first = 1:: and
code::spacing = 1:: the spectra agree, while BlipSeries also supports gapped,
offset, and fractional-ratio series.

classmethods::

method:: ar

argument:: freq
Fundamental frequency in Hz. Audio or control rate; signed values are valid.

argument:: numPartials
Requested partial count, sampled once per block and clipped to code::1..2048::
before alias limiting.

argument:: first
First partial ratio. Audio or control rate; values below zero become zero.

argument:: spacing
Spacing between partial ratios. Audio or control rate; values below zero
become zero.

argument:: mul
Post-processing multiplier; it does not affect phase or limiting.

argument:: add
Post-processing offset; it does not affect phase or limiting.

examples::

code::
(
{ BlipSeries.ar(80, 24, 1, 2, 0.1) }.play;
)
::

code::
(
{ BlipSeries.ar(70, 32, 6, SinOsc.ar(0.1).range(0, 0.25), 0.1) }.play;
)
::

code::
// Modulating all parameters for a dynamic sound
(
{ BlipSeries.ar(LFNoise1.kr(0.5).exprange(100, 400), LFNoise1.kr(0.5).range(1, 100), MouseX.kr(0, 5), MouseY.kr(0.5, 2.0)) ! 2 * 0.1 }.play;
)
::
